#**
A newsletter subscribe form, for themes that want one.

Call it with the weblog and a prompt:
    #showSubscribeForm($model.weblog "Get new guides by email")

Renders NOTHING when the weblog has no newsletter list configured (Weblog
Settings -> Newsletter list UUID), so themes call it unconditionally.

Emits only the placeholder slot; #showAudienceAssets injects the actual
form client-side and posts same-origin to the server-built data-endpoint
below (never a client-guessed /newsletter/subscribe -- that 404s under any
non-root context path, the same bug class #showAudienceAssets' contact slot
had), which THIS application serves (throttled, honeypotted, recorded as a
first-party event) and forwards to Listmonk. Roller stores no subscriber
data -- Listmonk records the address, sends the double opt-in email and owns
the unsubscribe link.
*#
#macro(showSubscribeForm $weblog $prompt)
#if($weblog.newsletterListUuid && $weblog.newsletterListUuid != "")
<div class="newsletter-subscribe-block">
    <p class="newsletter-prompt">$utils.escapeHTML($prompt)</p>
    <div class="subscribe-form-slot" data-list-uuid="$utils.escapeHTML($weblog.newsletterListUuid)"
         data-endpoint="$utils.escapeHTML($url.site)/newsletter/subscribe"></div>
</div>
#end
#end


#**
The comments section of an entry page. Each bundled theme's permalink.vm
calls it under the entry:
    #showComments($model.weblog $model.weblogEntry)

Renders NOTHING when the weblog has comments off (Weblog Settings), so themes
call it unconditionally. Otherwise it renders the PUBLISHED top-level
comments, oldest first, each with its PUBLISHED reply (the owner's, marked as
the author's); the count in the heading; and below them either "Comments are
closed" or the inert comments-slot that the showAudienceAssets macro's script
turns into the comment form.

Nothing in here may depend on who is looking. The page is cached and shared
by every visitor, so the form, the reader's name and the reader's own pending
comments come from the session endpoint at view time, never from this markup.
That is also why the endpoints are server-built ($utils.commentEndpoints:
the script never guesses the context path) and why a custom-domain weblog,
whose host does not carry the site's session cookie, gets a slot that says
"unavailable" instead of endpoints -- decided from the weblog, not the
request, because both hosts share one cached page.

Escaping: a display name is user-typed and stored raw, so it is escaped here;
the body is already-safe HTML from CommentBodyRenderer and is emitted bare.
Both are bidi-isolated (unicode-bidi: isolate), so an RTL override typed in
one cannot reorder the text around it.
No username appears here (an owner's is their login name): the page script
finds the reader's own comments by the ids the session endpoint returns,
matched against id="comment-<id>".
The styles use classes only: an id selector in this block would put a hash
before a word, which Velocity can read as a directive or a macro call.
*#
#macro(showComments $weblog $entry)
#if($entry && $weblog.commentsEnabled)
<style>
.comments { margin: 3rem 0 0; max-width: 42rem; }
.comments h2 { font-size: 1.25em; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
.comments .comment { margin: 0; padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(127, 127, 127, .3); }
.comments .comment header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: .25rem .6rem; font-size: .9em; }
.comments .comment-name { font-weight: 600; unicode-bidi: isolate; }
.comments .comment-badge { font-size: .75em; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase;
  padding: 0 .5em; border: 1px solid currentColor; border-radius: 1em; }
.comments time { opacity: .75; }
.comments .comment-body { overflow-wrap: anywhere; unicode-bidi: isolate; }
.comments .comment-body p { margin: .5rem 0; }
.comments .comment-reply { margin: .75rem 0 0 1.25rem; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 2px solid rgba(127, 127, 127, .4); }
.comments .comments-closed { font-style: italic; opacity: .85; }
.comments .comments-slot { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
.comments .comment-pending { opacity: .8; }
.comments .comment-pending .comment-body { white-space: pre-wrap; }
.comments .comment-whoami { font-size: .9em; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
.comments .comment-form textarea { display: block; width: 100%; min-height: 6em; padding: .4em; box-sizing: border-box; font: inherit; }
.comments .comment-form button { margin-top: .5rem; padding: .4em 1.2em; }
.comments .comment-message { margin: .75rem 0 0; }
.comments .comment-delete { margin-left: auto; padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; color: inherit;
  font: inherit; font-size: .85em; text-decoration: underline; cursor: pointer; }
</style>
<section class="comments" id="comments" aria-labelledby="comments-heading">
  <h2 id="comments-heading">$text.get("comments.heading", [$entry.commentCount])</h2>
  #foreach($c in $entry.comments)
  <article class="comment#if($c.authorIsOwner) comment-author#end" id="comment-$c.id">
    <header><span class="comment-name">$utils.escapeHTML($c.displayName)</span>#if($c.authorIsOwner) <span class="comment-badge">$text.get("comments.authorBadge")</span>#end
      <time datetime="$utils.formatIso8601Date($c.created)">$utils.formatDate($c.created, $text.get("comments.dateFormat"))</time></header>
    <div class="comment-body">$c.bodyHtml</div>
    #if($c.reply)
    <div class="comment-reply comment-author" id="comment-$c.reply.id">
      <header><span class="comment-name">$utils.escapeHTML($c.reply.displayName)</span> <span class="comment-badge">$text.get("comments.authorBadge")</span>
        <time datetime="$utils.formatIso8601Date($c.reply.created)">$utils.formatDate($c.reply.created, $text.get("comments.dateFormat"))</time></header>
      <div class="comment-body">$c.reply.bodyHtml</div>
    </div>
    #end
  </article>
  #end
  #if($entry.commentsClosed)
  <p class="comments-closed">$text.get("comments.closed")</p>
  #elseif($utils.isNotEmpty($weblog.customDomain))
  <div class="comments-slot" data-unavailable="custom-domain" data-msg-unavailable="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.unavailableHere"))"></div>
  #else
  <div class="comments-slot" data-entry="$entry.id" data-permalink="$utils.escapeHTML($entry.relativePermalink)"
       data-session="$utils.escapeHTML($utils.commentEndpoints.session)" data-post="$utils.escapeHTML($utils.commentEndpoints.post)"
       data-delete="$utils.escapeHTML($utils.commentEndpoints.delete)"
       data-msg-sign-in="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.signIn"))" data-msg-unavailable="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.unavailableHere"))"
       data-msg-pending="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.pending"))" data-msg-awaiting="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.awaiting"))"
       data-msg-published="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.published"))" data-msg-error="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.error"))"
       data-msg-rate="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.rateLimited"))" data-msg-signed-in-as="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.signedInAs"))"
       data-msg-account="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.yourAccount"))" data-msg-delete="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.deleteOwn"))"
       data-msg-delete-confirm="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.deleteOwn.confirm"))" data-msg-post="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.post"))"
       data-msg-delete-failed="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.deleteOwn.failed"))" data-msg-closed="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.closed"))"
       data-msg-not-allowed="$utils.escapeHTML($text.get("comments.notAllowed"))"></div>
  #end
</section>
#end
#end


#**
The visible business card, for theme footers. Call it with the weblog and
the theme's own booking-button wording:
    #showBusinessCard($model.weblog "Book a stay")

Renders NOTHING when the blog has neither a business nor a place, so themes
call it unconditionally. It shows the same facts the business JSON-LD
declares (Google expects structured data to describe visible content): the
name, a locality line, the phone as a tel: link and, when a booking URL
resolves, a UTM-tagged button carrying the Umami click attributes. The entry
anchor is passed on a permalink so the click is attributed to that entry.
Every value is escaped here; the model hands back raw strings.
*#
#macro(showBusinessCard $weblog $bookLabel)
#set($cardSlug = "")
#if($model.permalink && $model.weblogEntry)
#set($cardSlug = $model.weblogEntry.anchor)
#end
#set($card = false)
#set($card = $utils.businessCard($weblog.pojo, $cardSlug))
#if($card && !$card.isEmpty())
<aside class="business-card">
    #if($card.name)<p class="business-card-name">$utils.escapeHTML($card.name)</p>#end
    #if($card.locality)<p class="business-card-locality">$utils.escapeHTML($card.locality)</p>#end
    #if($card.telHref)<a class="business-card-tel" href="$utils.escapeHTML($card.telHref)">$utils.escapeHTML($card.telephone)</a>#end
    #if($card.bookingHref)<a class="business-card-book" href="$utils.escapeHTML($card.bookingHref)" rel="noopener" target="_blank" data-umami-event="business-card-click"#if($card.dest) data-umami-event-dest="$utils.escapeHTML($card.dest)"#end#if($cardSlug && $cardSlug != "") data-umami-event-entry="$utils.escapeHTML($cardSlug)"#end>$utils.escapeHTML($bookLabel)</a>#end
</aside>
#end
#end
